    "question": {
      ":question/id": "69a4f90c-41e3-5447-822d-c39dcc161500",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $1\\text{st}$ and $4\\text{th}$ rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $1\\text{st}$ and $4\\text{th}$ rows of $A$ are $2$ and $9$, respectively.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the answer is $2+9=11.$",
